    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78">

                <pb facs="0320" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v05/pg280"/>

                <head>78. Memorandum From the Director of the Executive Secretariat (Calhoun) to the
                    President’s Staff Secretary (Goodpaster)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d78-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-04-28"><hi rendition="#italic">April 28,
                        1960</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Follow-up Actions from the President’s Good Will Trip to South
                        America</item>
                </list>
                <p>You approved on March 30 the list of follow-up actions arising from the
                    President’s trip which I sent you with my memorandum of March 22.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d78-f2"/></p>
                <pb facs="0321" n="281" xml:id="pg281"/>
                <p>The enclosed report describes the status to date and future actions contemplated
                    with respect to these follow-up items.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d78-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">John A. Calhoun</hi><anchor n="4"
                            xml:id="d78-f4"/></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d78-a1.xml" xpointer="d78-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d78-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d78-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 711.11–EI/4–2860. Secret. Drafted by
                    Arthur R. Day of the Executive Secretariat’s Reports and Operations Staff on
                    April 27.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d78-f2" n="2" xml:id="d78-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed. (<hi rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., 711.11–EI/3–2260)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d78-f3" n="3" xml:id="d78-f3-content">
                <p>According to a handwritten notation on the source text, Goodpaster on May 4
                    informed officials of the Department of State that he approved the contents of
                    the enclosed report.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d78-f4" n="4" xml:id="d78-f4-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that bears this stamped signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
